WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:05.580
How did three petty criminals launch a&nbsp;
business empire, land a Guinness World Record,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:10.740
and become hallucinations of themselves? It&nbsp;
all started in a little place called Sunnyvale.

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:15.360
While it may appear that the show's central&nbsp;
trailer park has always looked the same,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:20.640
the first four seasons of Trailer Park Boys were&nbsp;
filmed at different locations across Nova Scotia,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.200
Canada. Due to complaints by the residents,&nbsp;
the boys were supposedly forced out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:28.740
these parks and eventually opted to&nbsp;
purchase and build their own set in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.060
Dartmouth. This is the park which fans&nbsp;
started seeing from season 5 onwards.

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:34.740
"It's a terrible situation."

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:39.780
Of course, the spin-off series, Out of the&nbsp;
Park, sees the characters Ricky, Julian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:44.880
and Bubbles going on adventures, making stops&nbsp;
in Europe and the United States. But while the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:49.320
trio have gone international, the true home&nbsp;
of the Boys is their eponymous trailer park.

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:55.440
There's been plenty of speculation surrounding&nbsp;
the departure of Jonathan Torrens' J-Roc from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.520
the show. Torrens announced his&nbsp;
departure via Twitter on April 20,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.520 --> 00:01:03.000
2016, and later said in his&nbsp;
podcast, Taggart and Torrens,

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:06.360
"I ultimately felt that I had&nbsp;
achieved all that I could with J-Roc,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:09.960
but he's been in my head and part of&nbsp;
my existence for so long, it's weird."

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:15.120
Although fans would love to see their favorite&nbsp;
rapper drop more bars at park concerts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:17.760
Torrens insists gave the role everything he had.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.940
The show's theme song is tranquil and gives&nbsp;
fans a peaceful view of the park before the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.940 --> 00:01:29.340
F-bombs and complete comedic chaos takes&nbsp;
over. It was directly influenced by singer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.340 --> 00:01:33.360
Tony Bennett's signature song, "I Left&nbsp;
My Heart in San Francisco," which peaked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:39.480
at No. 19 on the Billboard Hot 100 when&nbsp;
originally released in 1962. And in 2001,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:43.800
the tune peaked at No. 1 in the hearts&nbsp;
of Trailer Park Boys fans when "I Left&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.800 --> 00:01:48.480
My Heart in San Francisco" was adapted by&nbsp;
Blain Morris into the theme song "Breeze."

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:52.860
Although fans probably prefer calling it&nbsp;
simply the Trailer Park Boys Theme Song,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:56.760
from Bennett to Morris, the song&nbsp;
has and will always be a classic.

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:02.760
While it can be more rewarding to watch a&nbsp;
continuous, overarching story from start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:06.900
to finish — since audiences get to see&nbsp;
character development, minor story arcs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:10.980
and the plot pay off — Trailer Park&nbsp;
Boys is meant to be episodic. People&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:14.640
should be able to watch any episode&nbsp;
and still understand what's happening.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.060
"If you guys come back short, you're gonna&nbsp;
be responsible. Do you understand me?"

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.260
"I'm not stupid, Julian."

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.240
"Yes, you are stupid. That's&nbsp;
why I have to tell you this."

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:26.340
There are running jokes that any diehard&nbsp;
fan will appreciate, such as Randy's "shirt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.200
allergy," but a first-time viewer should be able&nbsp;
to watch any episode and understand the plot.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:35.520
But episodic or not, watching the&nbsp;
show in chronological order allows&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:38.520
viewers to better understand&nbsp;
the characters. On the surface,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:42.420
the Boys are just criminals who routinely&nbsp;
come up with small-minded plans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:48.180
break laws and wind up in jail. But as episodes&nbsp;
build on one another, Ricky, Julian, Bubbles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.620
and the rest of the park residents become&nbsp;
more charismatic, redeemable, and root-worthy.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.740
Jimmy Buffett has Margaritaville, Mark&nbsp;
Wahlberg has Wahlburgers, and Bubbles had&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:04.260
Bubbles Mansion. Unfortunately, they had to&nbsp;
close their doors in 2010. According to CBC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:09.000
manager Brad Hartlin said the Halifax bar&nbsp;
could no longer compete because students&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:13.740
stopped coming once legislation forced&nbsp;
minimum drink prices up from $1 to $2.50.

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.920
Although eight Liquor Control Act violations&nbsp;
had also hit their other bar, The Toothy Moose,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.920 --> 00:03:22.980
Hartlin claimed the closing of&nbsp;
Bubbles Mansion wasn't related&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.980 --> 00:03:27.360
to these legal troubles. No matter the&nbsp;
reasoning, Trailer Park Boys was — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:30.780
still is — famous enough for their&nbsp;
characters to open a bar in their name.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:36.720
The characters Jim and Barbara Lahey had&nbsp;
a daughter named Treena. Though she didn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:42.180
make many appearances throughout the series, they&nbsp;
might recognize her now famous actor: Elliot Page.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.180 --> 00:03:47.820
While Page has gone on to star in major Hollywood&nbsp;
projects like Juno, Inception, and The Umbrella&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.820 --> 00:03:52.920
Academy, he walked onto the Trailer Park Boys set&nbsp;
as an unknown and left as a beloved character.

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:55.740
"Would you be upset if your mom and Sam broke up?"

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:58.740
"Would Randy be upset if you&nbsp;
gave him a double cheeseburger?"

00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:02.700
Treena would visit Mr. Lahey in the&nbsp;
summers and befriended Ricky despite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.320
her father telling her to stay away from him&nbsp;
and Julian. While Page only appeared in a few&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:11.040
episodes in Season 2, Treena is mentioned&nbsp;
affectionately throughout the series.

00:04:12.360 --> 00:04:17.340
John Dunsworth — who played the fan-favorite&nbsp;
character Jim Lahey — passed away from an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:23.520
unexpected illness at 71 years old in 2017.&nbsp;
His daughter, Sarah Dunsworth-Nickerson – who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:27.060
also plays the character of Sarah on&nbsp;
the show – announced the sad news of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.620
her father's passing via Twitter on&nbsp;
October 16, 2017. The tweet read,

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:36.000
"With heavy and broken hearts the family&nbsp;
of John F. Dunsworth would like to let&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.920
people know that our amazing husband,&nbsp;
father and John Dunsworth has passed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:44.880
away. John left this world peacefully&nbsp;
after a short and unexpected illness."

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:49.380
After Dunsworth's death, the Season&nbsp;
12 finale concluded with a heartfelt&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:52.980
tribute to Dunsworth as well as&nbsp;
some eerie words from Mr. Lahey,

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:59.760
"When you're dead, you're dead. But you're not&nbsp;
quite so dead if you contribute something."

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.660
In the first episode of Trailer&nbsp;
Park Boys: The Animated Series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.660 --> 00:05:07.920
Mr. Lahey is carried off by a hawk,&nbsp;
which is probably the perfect ending&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.040
to a character who's always been&nbsp;
dropping isms related to hawks.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:16.980
Donny, the neighbor who's always screaming&nbsp;
off-camera at the boys, might sound familiar.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:21.420
That's because the character is the voice&nbsp;
of Mike Smith. While Donny might appear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:26.160
to unleash a whole lot of unnecessary rip-roaring&nbsp;
monologues, he sometimes does it for good reason.

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:30.300
"Donny, watch your language!&nbsp;
There are children in this park."

00:05:30.300 --> 00:05:35.760
Instead of being a wordless bystander, Donny&nbsp;
takes direct action by yelling uncontrollably&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.760 --> 00:05:40.500
at loud noises — such as crashing cars and&nbsp;
gunshots. We've all got a breaking point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.900
and sometimes a person just wants peace and quiet.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.900
While Donny is finally seen on-camera in&nbsp;
Season 12 his face is blurred out. His voice,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:52.380
which could use a bar of soap or&nbsp;
two, is still performed by Smith.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:58.740
While Julian always wears the same outfit of&nbsp;
a black shirt and blue jeans — usually while&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:03.300
holding a rum and coke — Ricky wearing the&nbsp;
same exact shirt throughout each season is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:07.140
to a different effect, even ending up&nbsp;
ripped or duct-taped in some seasons.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:11.940
While Ricky does change his clothes the running&nbsp;
joke is that he has an extremely limited number&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.940 --> 00:06:16.140
of shirts. Usually using one shirt per&nbsp;
season keeps this joke rolling, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:16.140 --> 00:06:20.880
wear and tear give his wardrobe that authentic,&nbsp;
Ricky-really-only-does-have-a-few-shirts feel..

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:26.580
It may be hard today to believe Trailer&nbsp;
Park Boys originally ended after seven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.580 --> 00:06:31.740
seasons. When Netflix took over in 2014,&nbsp;
they added five more seasons — as well&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:35.400
as specials, an animated series,&nbsp;
and multiple feature-length films.

00:06:35.400 --> 00:06:38.580
The Netflix deal came on the&nbsp;
heels of Wells, Tremblay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.580 --> 00:06:42.840
and Smith acquiring the rights to the show&nbsp;
from original producers Mike Clattenburg,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.840 --> 00:06:46.980
Barrie Dunn, and Mike Volpe. In&nbsp;
a statement, Clattenburg claimed,

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:51.720
"While the three of us have moved on to different&nbsp;
TV and film projects, the Boys are the only ones&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.720 --> 00:06:56.460
with the intimate knowledge and love of the&nbsp;
show to keep Trailer Park Boys alive and well."

00:06:56.460 --> 00:06:59.760
Not only has Netflix helped bring new life to TPB,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:59.760 --> 00:07:02.580
but they have brought the show&nbsp;
to a vastly wider audience.

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:09.180
SwearNet — created by Wells, Tremblay, and Smith&nbsp;
— features the entire world of Trailer Park Boys,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:14.340
and has become a true business empire,&nbsp;
creating its own beer, whiskey, and much more.

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.560
"He said he was really impressed with the customer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:20.160
service, and the beer's going great,&nbsp;
man. People are f—ing loving it!"

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:20.700
"Yeah!"

00:07:20.700 --> 00:07:22.440
"And he wants more."

00:07:22.440 --> 00:07:26.820
The website features clips of the Trailer&nbsp;
Park Boys family doing what they do best,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.820 --> 00:07:31.140
as well as clips capturing Wells,&nbsp;
Tremblay, and Smith out of character. Plus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:35.040
it even has its own movie — titled&nbsp;
Swearnet: The Movie — which holds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:38.760
the current Guinness World Record for the&nbsp;
most uses of the F-word in movie history.

00:07:40.320 --> 00:07:45.540
Creating an animated spinoff of a pre-existing,&nbsp;
live-action television series is nothing new.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:50.880
Star Trek, and the Canadian comedy Corner&nbsp;
Gas turned to cartoons to tell stories that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.880 --> 00:07:54.000
would have been difficult with their&nbsp;
flesh-and-blood actors. To this end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:59.160
in 2019, Trailer Park Boys: The Animated&nbsp;
Series debuted on Netflix as a direct&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.160 --> 00:08:02.760
follow-up to the original series, which&nbsp;
had just completed its 12th season.

00:08:02.760 --> 00:08:07.800
According to The Cord, the franchise going&nbsp;
animated was an in-universe plot development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:12.600
choice. At the end of Season 12, a gaggle of&nbsp;
characters were arrested for participating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.600 --> 00:08:17.100
in a drug smuggling operation, right after&nbsp;
they collectively consumed pounds of magic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:20.760
mushrooms. As the hallucinogenic&nbsp;
effects of those mushrooms kick in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:24.360
the characters start to see themselves&nbsp;
and their world as a giant cartoon.

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:30.000
Additionally, transitioning to an animated format&nbsp;
allowed the production to address the death of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:34.920
John Dunsworth. The producers opted to initially&nbsp;
keep Mr. Lahey alive in the animated series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:39.960
constructing his dialogue from old voice lines&nbsp;
recorded for episodes of the live-action series.

00:08:41.220 --> 00:08:45.840
Trailer Park Boys was one of those early&nbsp;
series which helped pioneer the mockumentary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:50.700
format in comedic television. Well before The&nbsp;
Office, Modern Family, or Abbott Elementary,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:50.700 --> 00:08:56.100
the Canadian series aimed to produce a seemingly&nbsp;
realistic look at life of petty criminals in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.100 --> 00:09:00.300
trailer park community. The characters were&nbsp;
acutely aware of the cameras in their faces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:04.140
and would comment on how they were being&nbsp;
filmed for a documentary. According to The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:08.340
Globe and Mail — to keep this idea going&nbsp;
— the three main stars of the show rarely&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:12.420
appear in public or give interviews&nbsp;
out of character or out of costume.

00:09:12.420 --> 00:09:13.500
"I'm Bubbles."

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:14.460
"I'm Julian."

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:19.260
"Am I…? I'm Ricky, but my passport says Randy&nbsp;
Lahey, so I'm not really sure who I am."

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:24.660
Smith, Wells, and Tremblay have received awards,&nbsp;
appeared on talk shows, and performed live as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.520
their Trailer Park Boys personas. They refuse&nbsp;
to break character in behind-the-scenes footage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:35.700
available as DVD extras, and in 2019, the trio&nbsp;
set sail on a Trailer Park Boys-themed cruise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:39.180
playing their roles for five straight&nbsp;
days while mingling with fans.

00:09:40.440 --> 00:09:43.980
The titular trailer park trio&nbsp;
might be petty ne'er-do-wells,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.980 --> 00:09:47.640
but offscreen, the franchise's&nbsp;
actors and creative forces have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:51.540
used their popularity and influence to&nbsp;
push for social and legislative change.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:57.540
In May 2021, Wells, Smith, and Tremblay starred&nbsp;
in a 50-second public service announcement for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.540 --> 00:10:02.220
Nova Scotia's department of health, titled Part of&nbsp;
Our Way Forward, where they advocate for getting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.220 --> 00:10:08.040
the COVID-19 vaccination. In March 2022, the&nbsp;
Boys produced and posted to Twitter a video&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:12.660
to bring awareness to the issue of poor quality&nbsp;
drinking water in indigenous Canadian communities,

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:18.000
"Government, just fix the indigenous water&nbsp;
problem would ya? It's not that hard."

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:18.660
"Please."

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:19.560
"Fix it, please!"

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:25.500
According to HuffPost, back in 2016, the Nova&nbsp;
Scotia government did away with a tax credit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.500 --> 00:10:30.300
that encouraged films and TV shows to shoot&nbsp;
in the province. Since the TPB production&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:35.700
was a beneficiary of that program, the Boys&nbsp;
waged the #SaveSunnyvale campaign on social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.700 --> 00:10:41.340
media in protest. Smith made a video, as Bubbles,&nbsp;
warning audiences that their show could possibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.340 --> 00:10:46.860
end without these financial advantages, and&nbsp;
days later, a $10 million production fund was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:52.740
established. Reportedly, $810,000 of this fund&nbsp;
went to fund Season 10 of Trailer Park Boys.

00:10:53.880 --> 00:10:59.340
The show's Canadian pride is often reflected&nbsp;
in the music used throughout the franchise — a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.340 --> 00:11:02.640
lot of the needle drops go to some&nbsp;
of Canada's most successful acts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:07.560
such as Rush, the Tragically Hip, and&nbsp;
April Wine. Some Canadian music legends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:07.560 --> 00:11:10.380
have even physically appeared&nbsp;
on Trailer Park Boys projects.

00:11:10.380 --> 00:11:13.140
"Randy cheated and stole his answer."

00:11:13.140 --> 00:11:15.660
"That's right, Alex. I'm&nbsp;
a way bigger fan than him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.460
You're the best guitar player that ever lived."

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:22.620
Per the CBC, in 2003, the primary&nbsp;
trio served as an opening act on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.620 --> 00:11:27.120
package tour with Canadian bands Finger&nbsp;
Eleven and Our Lady Peace. And in 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:33.420
Quebec-based EDM artist Marc Mysterio remixed&nbsp;
Bubbles' signature folk tune. Mike Smith has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:38.700
also popped up as Bubbles in videos by rap-reggae&nbsp;
artist Snow and rock band The Tragically Hip.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:44.580
According to Sleaze Roxx, in 2019, the Boys staged&nbsp;
a full-length concert at the Hair in the Fair&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.580 --> 00:11:50.820
Festival in Welland, Ontario, assisted by Canadian&nbsp;
hair metal figure Sebastian Bach of Skid Row. This&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:50.820 --> 00:11:55.860
wasn't too surprising as Bach has appeared as&nbsp;
himself on multiple Trailer Park Boys projects.

00:11:56.700 --> 00:12:01.740
Trailer Park Boys isn't just a single show,&nbsp;
evolving through several formats with new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:07.440
methods. After seven seasons on Canada's Showcase&nbsp;
network, the feature films Countdown to Liquor Day&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.440 --> 00:12:12.360
and Don't Legalize It were produced and then&nbsp;
released in Canadian movie theaters in 2009&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:12.360 --> 00:12:17.820
and 2014 respectively, bridging the original&nbsp;
show with the Netflix series revival in 2014.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:22.980
After 50 more episodes on the streaming&nbsp;
service, Trailer Park Boys evolved into two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:22.980 --> 00:12:27.480
seasons' worth of the animated series, and then&nbsp;
returned to live-action with Trailer Park Boys:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:27.480 --> 00:12:33.480
Jail. Distributed by SwearNet, the 2021&nbsp;
series of 10 episodes finds the criminally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:38.400
mischievous Ricky, Julian, and Bubbles in&nbsp;
a familiar place — prison. But this time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:43.620
it's a semi-permanent situation. While the trio&nbsp;
usually don't leave the Sunnyvale Trailer Park,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:43.620 --> 00:12:46.620
they're prohibited from leaving the&nbsp;
Sunnyvale Correctional Facility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:50.220
where it's considerably harder for them&nbsp;
to get up to their usual shenanigans.

